---
// The tools, for students and instructors. Outside the docs collection on
// purpose: out of the sitemap and search, linked from the About sidebar group,
// and an instructor tool is free to name Canvas (docs/agents/tools.md).
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    editUrl: false,
    head: [{ attrs: { content: "noindex", name: "robots" }, tag: "meta" }],
    pagefind: false,
    title: "Tools",
  }}
>
  <p>
    These tools read your files in your browser. Nothing is uploaded: the
    files never leave the page.
  </p>
  <h2>For Students</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/tools/submission-pdf/">Build your submission PDF</a>: your
      Markdown files and their images, with the cover lines, saved as the one
      PDF a submission needs.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>For Instructors</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/tools/peer-evaluation/">Peer evaluation</a>: prepare the
      Qualtrics survey, its contact list, and its email from the Canvas
      roster; then score the export into the rubric assessment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/tools/partner-evaluation/">Project partner evaluation</a>:
      prepare the Midterm Pulse or a term's End-of-Term Survey, its contact
      list, and its email from the Canvas roster and the partner sheet; then
      score the export into the rubric assessment and the concerns table.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/tools/defense-scoresheets/">Defense scoresheets</a>: print a
      session cover for each team and a one-page live sheet for each student
      from the Canvas roster, with the rubric's questions, items, and red
      flags word for word.
    </li>
  </ul>
</StarlightPage>
